# The video-metrics module's own texts: its name and the line under it, the
# way to the app, the hints of its two marks, and its page — the last scan,
# as the catalogue recorded it.
brain-task-video-metrics = Scan the video channels
brain-task-video-metrics-does = Every six hours, asks YouTube what is new on the channels you added to Video metrics — first their feeds, then the details and thumbnails of a few videos at a time — and scores it. It needs the network and waits while there is none, skips a round while power saving is on, and stops at once if YouTube asks whether this is a robot. While it scans, a mark on the modeline says so; if the last scan failed for every channel, a red mark stays until a scan works.
brain-task-video-metrics-brief = Asks YouTube every six hours what is new on your channels, and scores it.
cmd-video-metrics-catalogue = Open Video metrics, in a window
video-metrics-brain-mark-scanning = Scanning your video channels
video-metrics-brain-mark-failed = The last video scan failed for every channel
video-metrics-brain-last = The last scan
video-metrics-brain-started = Started
video-metrics-brain-ended = Ended
video-metrics-brain-channels = Channels asked
video-metrics-brain-failed = Channels that failed
video-metrics-brain-added = Videos added
video-metrics-brain-never = Nothing has been scanned yet
